2026-09-27T10:01:03.7956911Z Description:
2026-09-27T10:01:03.7957397Z This PPA contains more recent Python versions packaged for Ubuntu.
2026-09-27T10:01:03.7957855Z 
2026-09-27T10:01:03.7958999Z Disclaimer: there's no guarantee of timely updates in case of security problems or other issues. If you want to use them in a security-or-otherwise-critical environment (say, on a production server), you do so at your own risk.
2026-09-27T10:01:03.7960328Z 
2026-09-27T10:01:03.7960456Z Update Note
2026-09-27T10:01:03.7960730Z ===========
2026-09-27T10:01:03.7961160Z Please use this repository instead of ppa:fkrull/deadsnakes.
2026-09-27T10:01:03.7961563Z 
2026-09-27T10:01:03.7961696Z Reporting Issues
2026-09-27T10:01:03.7961984Z ================
2026-09-27T10:01:03.7962414Z 
2026-09-27T10:01:03.7962650Z Issues can be reported in the master issue tracker at:
2026-09-27T10:01:03.7963191Z https://github.com/deadsnakes/issues/issues
2026-09-27T10:01:03.7963517Z 
2026-09-27T10:01:03.7963680Z Supported Ubuntu and Python Versions
2026-09-27T10:01:03.7964077Z ====================================
2026-09-27T10:01:03.7964328Z 
2026-09-27T10:01:03.7964544Z - Ubuntu 22.04 (jammy) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.10)
2026-09-27T10:01:03.7965096Z - Ubuntu 24.04 (noble) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.12)
2026-09-27T10:01:03.7965592Z - Ubuntu 26.04 (resolute) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.14)
2026-09-27T10:01:03.7966553Z - Note: Python 3.10 (jammy), Python3.12 (noble), Python3.14 (resolute) are not provided by deadsnakes as upstream ubuntu provides those packages.
2026-09-27T10:01:03.7967442Z 
2026-09-27T10:01:03.7967606Z Why some packages aren't built:
2026-09-27T10:01:03.7968225Z - Note: for 22.04+, older python versions requre libssl<3 so they are not currently built
2026-09-27T10:01:03.7969138Z - If you need these, reach out to asottile to set up a private ppa
2026-09-27T10:01:03.8052666Z 
2026-09-27T10:01:03.8053168Z The packages may also work on other versions of Ubuntu or Debian, but that is not tested or supported.
2026-09-27T10:01:03.8053789Z 
2026-09-27T10:01:03.8053913Z Packages
2026-09-27T10:01:03.8054195Z ========
2026-09-27T10:01:03.8054361Z 
2026-09-27T10:01:03.8056281Z The packages provided here are loosely based on the debian upstream packages with some modifications to make them more usable as non-default pythons and on ubuntu.  As such, the packages follow debian's patterns and often do not include a full python distribution with just `apt install python#.#`.  Here is a list of packages that may be useful along with the default install:
2026-09-27T10:01:03.8058354Z 
2026-09-27T10:01:03.8058704Z - `python#.#-dev`: includes development headers for building C extensions
2026-09-27T10:01:03.8059412Z - `python#.#-venv`: provides the standard library `venv` module
2026-09-27T10:01:03.8060481Z - `python#.#-distutils`: provides the standard library `distutils` module
2026-09-27T10:01:03.8061355Z - `python#.#-lib2to3`: provides the `2to3-#.#` utility as well as the standard library `lib2to3` module
2026-09-27T10:01:03.8062412Z - `python#.#-gdbm`: provides the standard library `dbm.gnu` module
2026-09-27T10:01:03.8063113Z - `python#.#-tk`: provides the standard library `tkinter` module
2026-09-27T10:01:03.8063701Z 
2026-09-27T10:01:03.8063852Z Third-Party Python Modules
2026-09-27T10:01:03.8064200Z ==========================
2026-09-27T10:01:03.8064412Z 
2026-09-27T10:01:03.8065971Z Python modules in the official Ubuntu repositories are packaged to work with the Python interpreters from the official repositories. Accordingly, they generally won't work with the Python interpreters from this PPA. As an exception, pure-Python modules for Python 3 will work, but any compiled extension modules won't.
2026-09-27T10:01:03.8067679Z 
2026-09-27T10:01:03.8068644Z To install 3rd-party Python modules, you should use the common Python packaging tools.  For an introduction into the Python packaging ecosystem and its tools, refer to the Python Packaging User Guide:
2026-09-27T10:01:03.8069934Z https://packaging.python.org/installing/
2026-09-27T10:01:03.8070245Z 
